h4.disabled Download stl for 3d printer
#sizeSelect
  p.
    Use our wizard to calibrate our software for your 3D-printer:
  button.btn.btn-primary.btn-block#startWizard Start wizard
  br
  p.
    If you already know your settings, choose them here:
  .row
    .col-sm-6
      select.form-control#studSizeSelect
    .col-sm-6
      select.form-control#holeSizeSelect
  br
#wizardStepIntro
  p.
    Every 3D-printer is different and produces slightly different 3D-printed objects.
    To ensure a good fit between the 3D-printed parts and your LEGO-bricks,
    we calibrate our software for your printer.
  p.
    For the calibration, download the #[a(href='download/testStrip.zip') test strip] and print it.
#wizardStepStuds
  p.
    Try to connect the test strip studs into a LEGO-brick. Which size fits best?
  .selectContainer
    img.dynamicImage#wizardStudImage(src='img/testStripWizard/studs/E.png')
    img.overlayImage#wizardTextOverlayStud(src='img/testStripWizard/studs/textOverlay.png')
    svg.hitMap(viewBox='0 0 800 800', preserveAspectRatio='xMidYMid meet')
      polygon.studHit(data-option='I', points='476,328 583,151 388,109 391,303')
      polygon.studHit(data-option='H', points='517,390 706,337 591,170 479,341')
      polygon.studHit(data-option='G', points='523,397 511,469 710,552 713,351')
      polygon.studHit(data-option='F', points='445,529 520,708 706,565 507,481')
      polygon.studHit(data-option='E', points='340,537 274,691 478,695 437,533')
      polygon.studHit(data-option='D', points='270,480 79,577 254,696 335,531')
      polygon.studHit(data-option='C', points='256,398 264,472 72,563 48,365')
      polygon.studHit(data-option='B', points='304,329 263,386 48,357 179,199')
      polygon.studHit(data-option='A', points='310,324 385,302 378,109 186,192')
  p.wizardSelect This size fits best:
    select.form-control#wizardStudSizeSelect
#wizardStepHoles
  p.
    Now connect the LEGO-brick studs into the test strip. Which size fits best?
  .selectContainer
    img.dynamicImage#wizardHoleImage(src='img/testStripWizard/holes/4.png')
    img.overlayImage#wizardTextOverlayHole(src='img/testStripWizard/holes/numberOverlay.png')
    svg.hitMap(viewBox='0 0 800 800', preserveAspectRatio='xMidYMid meet')
      polygon.holeHit(data-option='6', points='529,370 518,447 696,524 705,331')
      polygon.holeHit(data-option='8', points='396,270 472,294 581,146 388,104')
      polygon.holeHit(data-option='7', points='478,300 533,363 707,325 588,154')
      polygon.holeHit(data-option='5', points='444,506 521,719 687,527 510,454')
      polygon.holeHit(data-option='4', points='332,508 440,512 515,721 260,704')
      polygon.holeHit(data-option='3', points='258,448 329,508 251,704 72,537')
      polygon.holeHit(data-option='2', points='247,365 255,444 73,532 69,335')
      polygon.holeHit(data-option='1', points='300,296 252,358 76,329 202,174')
      polygon.holeHit(data-option='0', points='303,290 386,272 373,101 205,164')
  p.wizardSelect This size fits best:
    select.form-control#wizardHoleSizeSelect
#wizardStepFinished
  p.
    You're all set! If you don't change your 3D-printer's settings, you can re-use
    the calibration settings for further prints.
  p#calibrationResult
    | Your calibration settings:
    br
    strong#calibrationSettings A 4

#wizardButtons
  br
  .row
    .col-sm-6
      button.btn.btn-primary.btn-block#wizardBack
        span #[i.fa.fa-chevron-left] &nbsp;
        span#text Go back
    .col-sm-6
      button.btn.btn-primary.btn-block#wizardNext
        span#text Next step
        span &nbsp; #[i.fa.fa-chevron-right]
  br
